## SECTION 1 — PROJECT STRUCTURE REVIEW

### 1.1 Hybrid Feature/Component Split — Inconsistent Boundaries
**Severity: High**

The project has **both** `src/features/` and `src/components/` but the boundary between them is blurred and inconsistent:

```
src/features/bookUpdates/BookUpdatesPage.tsx   ← a full page (feature)
src/components/collection/CollectionDetail.tsx  ← also a full page (should be feature)
src/components/novelCard/CardBook.tsx           ← true shared UI component
```

`CollectionDetail.tsx` is a 548-line page component with its own data fetching, mutations, routing, and modals — yet it lives under `components/`. Meanwhile `BookUpdatesPage.tsx` correctly lives under `features/`.

**Impact**: Team members cannot predict where to find or place code. "Components" becomes a dumping ground. This gets exponentially worse with team growth.

**Correct approach**:
```
src/features/
  collection/
    CollectionDetailPage.tsx       ← page logic
    components/
      SortableBookCard.tsx
      AddBookToCollectionModal.tsx
      CollectionCommentSection.tsx
    hooks/
      useCollectionBooks.ts
    api/
      collectionApi.ts

  bookUpdates/
    BookUpdatesPage.tsx
    components/
      CalendarStrip.tsx
      TimelineBookCard.tsx
      BookUpdatesSwiper.tsx

src/components/                    ← truly shared, leaf-level UI
  ui/                              ← Button, Modal, Skeleton, etc.
  novelCard/
  navbar/
```

